## 3. Connecting Users and Servers

A "User Installation" is an installation of the Program that is made
available to a single individual user, on a private server or computer,
for their own personal or professional use.

A "User" is a single individual person. If a legal entity or
organization wishes to use the Software, they must obtain a separate
license or permission from Vadi360.

When you are acting as a User, this License gives you the right to:
- Install and run the software on your own servers
- Modify the software for your own use
- Run modified versions of the software for yourself or your organization
- Share your modifications with others only under this License

If you are running the software on a server to provide a service to
multiple users (other than yourself), you must:
- Make the complete source code of the modified software available to
  all those users under this License
- Make prominent notice that the software is available under AGPLv3
- Ensure all users receive a copy of this License

## 4. Collective Works

A "Collective Work" is a work that combines the Program with other
independent programs, in each case obtaining substantial contributions
to the combined work, and communicating the combined work to users
outside the system.

To "operate a Collective Work" means to run the Program as part of a
data center or server environment that serves multiple users.

If you operate a Collective Work, you must make the source code of the
collective work available to all those users under this License.

